Foveated single layer (0099): a composition refused for a reason that passes no longer turns the single layer off for
the session (bugfix round 0.7, round 3). 0099 latched `foveated_composer_failed` on every refusal, including the
composer's 250 ms wait for a slot still on the GPU after one long stall (or a refused call): the focus line and the
flicker of the two-layer submission then came back until DCS restarted. Now such a frame goes down as its two layers
(and so does a repeat of it: the composed image went back unwritten, but no frame names it) and the next fresh
submission composes again. Only what cannot be undone still latches: the composer or the composed swapchain cannot
be made, the image cannot be acquired, waited for (it stays acquired) or released. Flight log: foveated_mode
result=4 a=2 b=5 (c the refusals so far), written when the state changes, so a run of refusals is one record and the
return to composing (a=1) one more. Tests only: XRFG_TEST_FOVEATED_COMPOSE_REFUSALS=<n> refuses compositions 10 to
10 + n - 1; new test xrfg_layer_two_layers_deep_hold_composed_refused (alone): the refused frames go as two layers,
composed frames follow them, the log has the refusal record and composing twice.

